      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks this is good. one thing though, can you make it sound a little more firm? i feel like the current version is too soft, like i'm asking for a favor rather than pointing out a mistake they made. also we've had a few of these weird 'missing' volume issues lately with them, so i want to sound like we're really keeping a close eye on it now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version with a firmer tone:\n\nSubject: Discrepancy in Recent Shipment and Request for Credit Memo\n\nDear [Supplier's Name],\n\nI am writing to bring to your attention a discrepancy in our recent shipment of resin from your company. Our monthly invoice, which was received on [Date], shows a quantity of [Quantity] of resin, but upon inspection, we found that the actual quantity received was [Actual Quantity]. This discrepancy results in an overcharge of [Amount] on our invoice, and we expect a prompt correction.\n\nWe have experienced similar discrepancies in previous shipments, and it has become clear that there is a need for improved accuracy in your billing process. As a result, we require a credit memo to be issued immediately to rectify this situation. We expect a detailed explanation for the discrepancy in the quantity billed versus the quantity received, and we will be monitoring your response closely to ensure that this issue is addressed.\n\nWe expect a credit memo to be processed within the next [Timeframe, e.g. 3-5 business days] and for the overcharge to be waived. We will be reviewing our future orders with your company to ensure that this issue is not repeated.\n\nPlease confirm in writing that you",
